{
  "analysis": "I found the critical bug! In `execSpecial`, the JR and JALR instructions use `break` instead of `return` after calling `executeDelayAndJump`. This causes `this.pc` to be overwritten with `curPC + 4` (the delay slot address) instead of the jump target. The delay slot gets executed twice, and the PC falls through to the wrong location. This is why fwrite is called in a loop - JR doesn't return to the caller properly. I need to fix JR/JALR to `return` instead of `break`, and remove the trace code.",
  "plan": "Fix JR and JALR in execSpecial to use `return` instead of `break` after executeDelayAndJump. Remove the trace code. Then re-test the VM.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'
src=open('/app/vm.js').read()
# Fix JR: change break to return after executeDelayAndJump
src=src.replace('''      case 0x08: { // JR
        const target = this.r[rs] >>> 0;
        this.executeDelayAndJump((curPC + 4) >>> 0, target);
        break;
      }''', '''      case 0x08: { // JR
        const target = this.r[rs] >>> 0;
        this.executeDelayAndJump((curPC + 4) >>> 0, target);
        return;
      }''')
# Fix JALR: change break to return after executeDelayAndJump
src=src.replace('''      case 0x09: { // JALR
        const target = this.r[rs] >>> 0;
        this.setReg(rd === 0 ? 31 : rd, (curPC + 8) >>> 0);
        this.executeDelayAndJump((curPC + 4) >>> 0, target);
        break;
      }''', '''      case 0x09: { // JALR
        const target = this.r[rs] >>> 0;
        this.setReg(rd === 0 ? 31 : rd, (curPC + 8) >>> 0);
        this.executeDelayAndJump((curPC + 4) >>> 0, target);
        return;
      }''')
# Remove trace code
src=src.replace('''    // Trace fwrite calls
    if ((pc >>> 0) === 0x43a950 && this.instCount < 100000) {
      console.error(`[trace] fwrite called r4=${this.r[4]>>>0} r5=${this.r[5]>>>0} r6=${this.r[6]>>>0} r7=${this.r[7]>>>0} ra=${(this.r[31]>>>0).toString(16)} inst=${this.instCount}`);
    }
''', '')
src=src.replace('''    if (this.instCount < 100) console.error(`[trace] pc=${(pc>>>0).toString(16)} inst=${(inst>>>0).toString(16)} op=${(inst>>26)&0x3f} instCount=${this.instCount}`);
''', '')
src=src.replace('''    if (this.instCount < 100000) console.error(`[trace] syscall v0=${v0} a0=${a0} a1=${a1} a2=${a2} pc=${this.pc.toString(16)}`);
''', '')
open('/app/vm.js','w').write(src)
PY
node -c /app/vm.js
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -f /tmp/frame.bmp /tmp/vm_out.txt; timeout 30 node /app/vm.js > /tmp/vm_out.txt 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"; wc -l /tmp/vm_out.txt; head -40 /tmp/vm_out.txt; tail -10 /tmp/vm_out.txt; ls -la /tmp/frame.bmp 2>/dev/null
",
      "duration": 32.0
    }
  ]
}
